The family passes the conceptual screen: G is inverse-planted, V is one XOR recomputation, and H is the exact-weight \(Ax=b\) problem—NP-complete in general and W[1]-hard when weight is the parameter. I’ll avoid the paper’s easy constructions (independent sets and BCH-style structured codes), keep both the weight and syndrome dimension growing, and add a small seed-varying affine-dependency gadget solely so the relabelling-invariant diversity key is informative; planted and non-planted positions remain sampled identically.
