The family is exact-weight binary syndrome decoding, derived from Section 3’s \(h\)-linear combinations and Theorem 3.1’s code correspondence in the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.19413). Exact-weight binary \(Ax=b\) is NP-complete and W[1]-hard in the weight parameter ([Arvind et al.](https://www.sebastian-kuhnert.de/cs/paper/linearequations.pdf)).

Key results:

- All G1–G8 gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/250,000.
- Exact small-case density: 2/91,390.
- Six adversary attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Canonical key: 100/100 relabellings invariant; 20/20 unrelated instances distinct.
- Oracle verdict: `hardened`.
- The trivial demo was solved by all three oracles; the shipping `standard` preset failed against Claude Sonnet 5, Grok 4.6, and Gemini 3.1 Pro.
- Every oracle reply parsed, so no failure relied on a parser bug.
